course: dictionary
lesson: 14988
title: The word repository
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A repository is a place where things are stored and kept safe, so they can be found again later. Think of a cupboard or a store room. «The school library is a repository of over ten thousand books.» The library keeps the books safe, so anyone can come back and find them.
explain: In computing, a repository is a place where files are kept, often online. «Sam saved his game code in an online code repository so his team could help.» The repository keeps the project's files and their history, so the whole team can work on the same code. Programmers often shorten it to «repo».
explain: A person can be a repository too. «Grandma is a repository of family stories.» She holds a lot of stories in her head, so she is like a store of knowledge. To check your meaning, read the sentence again and swap in your idea: does it still make sense?
fact: A repository is a place where things are stored or kept safe.
fact: In computing, a repository stores files or code, often online.
fact: Programmers often shorten "repository" to "repo".
fact: «A repository of knowledge» means a person or book that holds a lot of facts and ideas.
fact: Repository is a noun, and its plural is repositories.
exercise: «The school library is a repository of over ten thousand books.» What is a repository here? | *A place where many things are stored and kept safe | A type of bookshelf that wobbles | A loud room where people shout | A book that is never read
exercise: Programmers say «repo» for short. What does a code repository store? | One photo from last summer | *Files and code for a project, along with its history | Hungry animals | Recipes for school lunch
exercise: «Grandma is a repository of family stories.» What does this suggest about Grandma? | *She holds lots of stories and knowledge | She always forgets things | She has no stories at all | She is a computer
test: «The museum is a repository of old objects from ancient Egypt.» What does repository mean here? | A tiny room with no windows | *A place where old objects are stored and kept safe | A shop that sells old objects | A game played with old toys
test: Ali says «Put your project in the code repository.» Where does the project go? | Under the bed | *Into a place online where the code files are stored | On a plate | In the bin
exam: Which word means a place, or a person or book, that holds a lot of stored knowledge or things? | Resting | Reply | *Repository | Repeat
